Hey @Socvest , thank you for opening this issue!

In general, we don't have an official way to support callbacks on custom components (https://github.com/streamlit/streamlit/issues/3977), but it looks like the latest release broke some workarounds that worked previously (https://github.com/victoryhb/streamlit-option-menu/issues/70). (I saw your comment under the last issue.) 

@raethlein could have more information about this, but as far as I understood, this particular case doesn't connect with `st.experimental_dialog` behavior.

@LukasMasuch Just fyi, the current plan is to have another release candidate (RC2) out this weekend and then the official release of Altair 5 around 08/09.05. If nothing comes up, the official release will be what is currently in master so you can use RC2 or the current master branch for testing.

Apart from the change to top-level import which is described further above in the issue, it would be awesome if the frontend could be upgraded to VL 5.7.1 I think it currently uses VL 5.6 and there have been some changes in 5.7 which are important for more complex charts in Altair such as layered repeat charts.

Update: RC2 is out now.

@Asaurus1 You're right, I totally missed that. Or rather, I forgot about it in the time between first looking at this issue and coming back to comment on it. I should have reviewed it first, instead of assuming from just the title.

I'm going to investigate this probably later today, but my hunch based on the behavior is that the frontend-backend desync is because the page change causes the frontend to drop its local state for the text input, but because that script run doesn't finish and clean up the state, the new script run with the text input thinks the frontend already has the state and so doesn't send it again.

If my hunch is correct, this will be tricky to fix, since the semantics of frontend and backend state interacting can be subtle and it would be easy to accidentally introduce a bug in the opposite direction. Maybe I can make the backend always send the state it knows about after a page change.
